  "_doc": "Foliage table (js/foliage.js). One row per original Octomancer FoliageItem (octomancer-unity Assets/ScriptableObjects/FGFoliageTiles and BGFoliage, extracted by octomancer-web/tools/extract_foliage.py). Unity fields are copied verbatim in Unity units (1 unit = 1 tile, y UP): pos = PositionOffset, rx / ry = RandomOffsetRangeX / Y, rot = RotationOffset, chance = SpawnChance (a Perlin threshold: a cell qualifies where the kind's noise is at least this, so 0.8 is rare and 0.4 common), max = MaxSpawned (times the level's DynamicDensity, (w/10 + h/16)/2, times capScale), fail = FailChance (0-100), noEdge = DontSpawnOnEdge, rand = the prefab's FoliageRandomizer [scale % min, max, rotation degrees] (only the BGFoliage prefabs carry one). Derived per row: size = the art's upright [w, h] in Unity units (prefab bounds), sink = how far the base sits inside the rock along the surface normal (Unity: pattern centre 0.5 + PositionOffset + the art's own extent; web y is DOWN, the code turns every offset into 'along the rim' and 'into the rock'). Web-only fields: surf (floor / ceiling / wall / hover / embed), base (the art edge that touches the rock: bottom / top / right), art (a cell of assets/foliage.webp, or @name for a separate image), h = a fixed height in tiles instead of size x sizeMul, vary = per-instance scale range, sway = sway amplitude in radians, mirror = floor art hung upside down from a ceiling. Unity items not spawned: Eye / Eye1 (background eyes), FoliageHole01/02 (the bullet-hole sprite), FoliageCritter2/4/6/7 (Creature-rig critters; 4 = jellyfish and 6/7 = snail were dropped by Daniel's round-3/4 reviews, 2 is a grey silhouette blob that only reads while its walk cycle plays). FoliageCritter1 is the open-water fish decor.js already spawns.",
